  <div class="source-note">
    <p>
      Here are a few concrete signals from official sources:
    </p>
    <ul class="rich-list">
      <li>
        The <a href="https://www.weforum.org/publications/the-future-of-jobs-report-2025" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">World Economic Forum Future of Jobs Report 2025</a> says labour markets through 2030 are being reshaped by technological change, demographic shifts, economic uncertainty, geoeconomic fragmentation, and the green transition.
      </li>
      <li>
        The U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics projects strong 2024 to 2034 growth for <a href="https://www.bls.gov/ooh/math/data-scientists.htm" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">data scientists</a> at 34%, <a href="https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/information-security-analysts.htm" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">information security analysts</a> at 29%, <a href="https://www.bls.gov/ooh/computer-and-information-technology/software-developers.htm" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">software developers</a> at 16%, and <a href="https://www.bls.gov/ooh/management/medical-and-health-services-managers.htm" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">medical and health services managers</a> at 23%.
      </li>
      <li>
        BLS also shows strong projected growth in clean-energy adjacent roles like <a href="https://www.bls.gov/ooh/construction-and-extraction/solar-photovoltaic-installers.htm" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">solar photovoltaic installers</a> at 42% and <a href="https://www.bls.gov/ooh/installation-maintenance-and-repair/wind-turbine-technicians.htm" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">wind turbine technicians</a> at 50%.
      </li>
      <li>
